Accessory brand <a href="https://alogic.co/?ref=y2uwzwu">Alogic</a> today announced an expansion to its display lineup, adding several new 5K and 6K models offering varying feature sets with availability coming over the next couple of months.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/alogic-aspekt-displays.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062541" /><em>Aspekt displays</em></div><br/>
New models in the Aspekt touch-enabled family include a 27-inch 5K model and a 32-inch 6K model with support for 10-point multitouch and MPP 2.0 styluses. Dock capabilities are built into the display, including USB-C with up to 90 watts of upstream charging, HDMI 2.1, DisplayPort 2.0, additional USB-C and USB-A ports, Gigabit Ethernet, and USB-A KVM functionality. There's also a 34-inch 5K Ultrawide model, which offers a resolution of up to 5,120 x 2,160 and a 100Hz refresh rate, plus the 10-point multitouch functionality<br/>
<br/>
The 27-inch 5K (&#36;1,899.99) and 32-inch 6K (&#36;2,999.99) models will be available by the end of October, while the 34-inch Ultrawide 5K model will be priced at &#36;2,799.99 and launch by the end of November.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/alogic-clarity-6k.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062543" /><em>Clarity 6K display</em></div><br/>
Alogic has also expanded its Clarity family of displays, adding a 12-megapixel webcam to the 27-inch 5K (&#36;1,899.99) and 32-inch 6K (&#36;3,099.99) models, with availability by the end of October. Both displays similarly offer touchscreen support, USB-C, HDMI 2.1, and DisplayPort 1.4 connectivity options, USB-A and audio connections, and up to 90 watts of upstream charging.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/alogic-vision-displays.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062545" /><em>Vision displays</em></div><br/>
There's also a new 34-inch Edge 5K Ultrawide option priced at &#36;1,599.99 launching by mid-November, and finally, on the low end of the display lineup, Alogic is introducing new 24-inch (&#36;199.99) and 27-inch (&#36;299.99) options in its Vision family of business-oriented displays, plus a 34-inch Ultrawide model.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/alogic-flashdock-5.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062546" /><em>FlashDock 5</em></div><br/>
Turning to peripherals, Alogic has announced the <a href="https://alogic.co/products/flashdock-5-13-in-1-thunderbolt-5-docking-station-with-ssd-support/?ref=y2uwzwu">FlashDock 5 docking station</a>, a 13-port Thunderbolt 5 dock supporting full bandwidth of up to 80 Gbps in symmetric mode or up to 120 Gbps in asymmetric mode. It supports up to three external displays (depending on capabilities of the host computer), with two HDMI 2.1 ports, two USB-C 3.2 Gen 2 ports, three USB-A ports, a 2.5 Gigabit Ethernet port, SD and microSD card readers, a 3.5mm combo audio port, and an additional downstream Thunderbolt 5 port. There's also an integrated M.2 NVMe SSD slot to allow you to add external storage. It's available now and is priced at &#36;399.99.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/alogic-crux-mouse.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062549" /><em>Crux mouse</em></div><br/>
And on the input side, Alogic is now shipping several previously announced accessories including the ergonomic multifunction Crux productivity mouse, priced at <a href="https://alogic.co/products/crux-usb-c-rechargeable-wireless-productivity-mouse/?ref=y2uwzwu">&#36;79.99</a>. The Hush full-size keyboard (<a href="https://alogic.co/products/hush-full-size-usb-c-rechargeable-wireless-keyboard-with-backlight/?ref=y2uwzwu">&#36;89.99</a>) with backlit keys and multi-device support is also shipping, as is the Hush mouse (<a href="https://alogic.co/products/hush-usb-c-rechargeable-wireless-mouse/?ref=y2uwzwu">&#36;29.99</a>) with a slim design and multi-device support.<br/>
